# {{ kb_title }}

{{ kb_description }}

This knowledge base is maintained mostly by LLM agents, following Karpathy's
[LLM wiki](https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f)
pattern. `{{ bundle_dir }}/` is a conformant
[Open Knowledge Format v0.2](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/open-knowledge-format/blob/main/SPEC.md)
bundle{% if obsidian %} and, at the same time, an [Obsidian](https://obsidian.md) vault{% endif %}.
Agents compile sources into pages; you curate sources, read and ask questions.

It was generated from the [okf-kb-template](https://github.com/egparedes/okf-kb-template)
copier template (answers in `.copier-answers.yml`). Run `copier update --trust`
to pull template changes. Full documentation:
<https://egparedes.github.io/okf-kb-template/>.

## Layout

```
AGENTS.md{% if claude_code %} / CLAUDE.md{% endif %}   conventions and workflows for agents
.agents/skills/         kb-ingest, kb-query, kb-maintain
schema/                 vocabulary (types, relations, extra fields), taxonomy (folders), resources, core frontmatter schema
tools/kbtools/          the `kb` CLI: check, index, fix-links, mv, merge, new, log, find, report,
                        graph, dupes, unlinked, zotero, karakeep, fetch, open
justfile                task runner (`just` lists recipes)
{{ (bundle_dir ~ '/').ljust(23) }} OKF bundle root{% if obsidian %} == Obsidian vault root{% endif %}
```

**Owned by this knowledge base:** `schema/vocabulary.yaml`,
`schema/taxonomy.yaml`, `schema/resources.yaml`, this README and everything
in `{{ bundle_dir }}/`.
Copier never overwrites these files.

**Managed by the template:** the rest (tooling, skills, AGENTS.md, CI).
Change them upstream and run `copier update`.

## Setup

Requirements: [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), [just](https://just.systems), git
{%- if obsidian %} and Obsidian 1.13.7 or later{% endif %}. Optional:
[lychee](https://lychee.cli.rs) (URL checks) and [qmd](https://github.com/tobi/qmd)
(hybrid search).

```sh
cp .env.example .env   # then fill in paths and keys for this machine
just setup             # git init if needed, uv sync, pre-commit, indexes
just ci                # kb check, independent OKF validator, tests, index freshness
```

`copier update` fetches the template from `_src_path` in
`.copier-answers.yml`. If that repository is private, git needs GitHub
credentials (e.g. `gh auth setup-git`).
{% if obsidian %}
Obsidian: open `{{ bundle_dir }}/`, not the repository root, as the vault.

```sh
just obsidian-setup          # installs the pinned community plugins
```

Then open `{{ bundle_dir }}/` with *Open folder as vault*, choose "Trust author and enable plugins", and in *Settings → Templater*
turn on "Trigger Templater on new file creation". Details are in
[docs/obsidian-setup.md](docs/obsidian-setup.md).
{% endif %}
To run `kb` from anywhere, or with several knowledge bases on one machine,
install the optional global launcher:
`uv tool install "git+https://github.com/egparedes/okf-kb-template#subdirectory=launcher"`.

## Daily use

Talk to your agent from the repository root:

- *"Ingest https://…"* compiles a source into the wiki (skill `kb-ingest`).
- *"What does the KB say about …?"* answers with citations and can file the
  answer back (skill `kb-query`).
- *"Lint the knowledge base"* runs checks and fixes structure (skill `kb-maintain`).

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `just check` | OKF v0.2 conformance and house rules |
| `just fix` | Normalize links to `/…` form and regenerate every `index.md` |
| `just validate-okf` | Independent OKF validator (okf-skills, pinned) |
| `just report` | Trust tiers, stale pages, uncited pages and wanted pages |
| `just find --type Concept --tag x` | Frontmatter queries |
| `just search "question"` | qmd hybrid search, falling back to ripgrep |
| `just health` | Link graph (index hubs excluded), duplicate candidates, unlinked mentions |
| `uv run kb mv old.md new.md` | Move a page and rewrite every inbound link |
| `uv run kb merge old.md into.md` | Fold a duplicate into another page (after merging the text) |
| `uv run kb zotero search …` / `kb fetch <ref>` | Zotero, KaraKeep and file roots: see [docs/external-resources.md](docs/external-resources.md) |
